# Deploying a Lovable (TanStack Start) App with GitHub Actions ...
created: 2026-07-18, last updated: 2026-07-21, [Read more](https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/deploying-lovable-tanstack-start-app-github-actions-real-shaterian-272he)

},
});
...
With Nitro's cloudflare-module preset (Lovable's default), the build output is a Worker bundle — .output/server/index.mjs — meant to render pages on demand, per request, inside Cloudflare's runtime.
...
Lovable's wrapper warns against adding a second nitro() plugin — but it turns out you can pass one through vite.plugins, and the wrapper is smart enough to treat it as an override rather than a duplicate:
```
import { defineConfig } from "@lovable.dev/vite-tanstack-config";
import { nitro } from "nitro/vite";
export default defineConfig({
tanstackStart: {
server: { entry: "server" },
prerender: {
enabled: true,
autoSubfolderIndex: true,
autoStaticPathsDiscovery: true,
crawlLinks: true,
},
},
vite: {
plugins: [nitro({ preset: "node-server" })],
},
});
```
...
